tatus":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Executive","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Resource and Finance Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Executive","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"West Surrey Shadow Authority Executive","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Shareholder Executive Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Woking's four-year audit backlog prevents finalization of recent accounts","lead":"Woking Council faces a significant backlog of unfinalized accounts spanning 2019/20 to 2022/23 \u2014 four financial years \u2014 still incomplete after six years. The external auditor BDO has issued a disclaimed opinion for 2019/20, meaning the auditor cannot confirm whether the accounts are fairly stated, the most serious audit outcome. An unresolved objection to those accounts is blocking finalization, and BDO cannot guarantee amendments will not be required. Until this backlog is cleared, the successor auditor cannot finalize accounts from 2023/24 onwards. The committee heard the completion of 2019/20 would be \"a significant milestone\" in clearing this historic backlog.","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"AUD26-039 BDO External Audits","paper_url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47642/47642.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Woking council's \u00a35.4m capital spending slips as homelessness costs pressure budget","lead":"Woking council is forecasting that \u00a35.4m of its approved capital spending will slip into future years, representing 15.6 per cent of the \u00a334.8m programme for 2026-27. The slippage is distributed across the General Fund and the housing revenue account (HRA), the separate, ring-fenced account for the council's own housing stock. Simultaneously, the council's homelessness service is facing an ongoing cost pressure of \u00a30.99m, driven by bed and breakfast expenditure for an average of 188 households \u2014 a figure that matches the five-year average, signalling a structural issue rather than temporary demand spike. The council's budget monitoring for the first quarter also identified a \u00a31.42m shortfall from the budgeted sale of Albion House, and delays to essential works at Pool in the Park that are costing the leisure service \u00a3180k in lost management fee income.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"EXE26-036 Budget Monitoring Q1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47622/47622.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"AUD26-039 BDO External Audits","paper_url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47642/47642.pdf","headline":"Unresolved objection to 2019/20 and 2020/21 accounts prevents audit finalization and introduces uncertainty about final conclusions.","detail":"An objection to the council's accounts is pending resolution. BDO has provided draft response to Public Sector Audit Appointments but cannot finalize the audit opinion until this process concludes. Critically, BDO states it \"cannot provide a guarantee that amendments will not be required before the audit opinion is finalised.\"","category":"audit","matters":"An unresolved objection and auditor uncertainty about final conclusions means the nature or magnitude of accounting issues is not yet settled, creating ambiguity about the council's actual financial position.","figures":"2019/20 and 2020/21 accounts affected","quote":"Members should note that BDO's audit opinion remains in draft form pending the resolution of an objection to the Council's 2019/20 and 2020/21 Statement of Accounts.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"AUD26-039 BDO External Audits","paper_url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47642/47642.pdf","headline":"Historic audit backlog blocking current audits: 2019/20 still unfinalized prevents 2023/24 onwards from being concluded.","detail":"The council is six years behind on account finalizations. Completion of 2019/20 is described as \"a significant milestone in progressing the Council's historic audit backlog\". Until BDO concludes 2019/20 to 2022/23, Grant Thornton (the successor auditor) cannot finalize 2023/24 onwards, keeping the council outside any timely audit cycle.","category":"governance","matters":"An inability to maintain a timely audit cycle and complete routine financial statement audits indicates systemic governance and financial management weaknesses affecting operational competence and financial control.","figures":"Backlog covers four years (2019/20 to 2022/23); current audit (2023/24 onwards) blocked","quote":"Grant Thornton will not be able to finalise the audits from 2023/24 onwards until BDO has concluded the audits for the periods 2019/20 to 2022/23.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","paper_title":"AUD26-039 BDO External Audits","paper_url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47642/47642.pdf","headline":"Disclaimed audit opinion for 2019/20 accounts signals major accounting record deficiency.","detail":"BDO has issued a disclaimed opinion rather than a qualified opinion, meaning the auditor cannot express whether the accounts are fairly stated. This typically reflects significant deficiencies in the council's accounting records or financial controls. The opinion remains in draft pending resolution of an objection to the 2019/20 and 2020/21 accounts.","category":"audit","matters":"A disclaimed opinion indicates fundamental weaknesses in financial record-keeping and control that would concern any lender assessing credit quality and governance capability.","figures":"2019/20 audit (six years from current date); 2020/21 also under objection","quote":"Following completion of their work, BDO have issued their final draft audit opinion, which is a disclaimed opinion attached as Appendix 1.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"EXE26-036 Budget Monitoring Q1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47622/47622.pdf","headline":"Pending \u00a3500m debt relief at 30 September 2026 carries timing risk and could shift outturn if delayed","detail":"The council has budgeted to receive \u00a3500m in debt relief at 30 September 2026. Treasury management explicitly notes 'any change in the timing of this transaction is likely to impact on the budget variance', indicating this is material to year-end position with timing dependency.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A material debt relief at period-end is subject to timing risk; if delayed past 30 September it would shift impact to 2027-28; the nature and counterparty of the relief are material to assessing debt sustainability","figures":"\u00a3500m debt relief due 30 September 2026","quote":"The Council has budgeted to receive \u00a3500m debt relief at 30 September 2026 and any change in the timing of this transaction is likely to impact on the budget variance","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"EXE26-036 Budget Monitoring Q1 2026-27","paper_url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47622/47622.pdf","headline":"HRA planned reserve contribution reduced 43%: from \u00a31.018m to \u00a30.577m due to \u00a30.441m overspend","detail":"The Housing Revenue Account is forecasting a \u00a30.441m overspend which reduces the planned reserve contribution from \u00a31.018m to \u00a30.577m. HRA reserves are forecast to reach \u00a37.595m at year-end, representing lower reserve accumulation than budgeted and reducing the buffer for future pressures.","category":"reserves","matters":"Lower reserve generation reduces financial resilience in the HRA; housing authorities depend on reserves to manage demand volatility and investment timing flexibility","figures":"\u00a31.018m budgeted reserve contribution reduced to \u00a30.577m (43% reduction), HRA reserves forecast \u00a37.595m","quote":"Due to this overspend, the planned contribution to reserves of \u00a31.018m will not be made in full. Instead, the HRA is forecast to contribute \u00a30.577m to its reserves","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-17"},"name":"Woking BC","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-26","since_iso":"2026-08-27","distress":false,"headline":"Unresolved objection to 2019/20 and 2020/21 accounts prevents audit finalization and introduces uncertainty about final conclusions.","lead":"An unresolved objection and auditor uncertainty about final conclusions means the nature or magnitude of accounting issues is not yet settled, creating ambiguity about the council's actual financial position.","also":["9 other findings in this window","3 papers caught"],"watch":"Executive on 2026-10-08","n_findings":10,"n_documents":3,"top_paper_title":"AUD26-039 BDO External Audits","top_paper_url":"https://woking.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47642/47642.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":125,"news_drafts_total":2}}